%[text] %[text:anchor:T_CAECB43A] # Introduction to Filtering
%[text] An introduction to simple filters and their applications to different types of signals.
%[text]{"align":"center"} ![Spectrogram after application of bandpass filter](text:image:8deb)
%[text:tableOfContents]{"heading":"Table of Contents"}
%%
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_44E16B04] ## Before you get started
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_BF646A47] This live script is intended to be used with the code hidden. On the **View** tab of the MATLAB® toolstrip, in the **View** section, select **Hide Code**.  Alternately, select **Hide Code** using the icon ![Hide code icon](text:image:3f36) at the top right of the Live Editor pane.
%[text] ![](text:image:709b) Although the code is hidden, some interactivity requires familiarity with MATLAB. If you need more instruction, consider taking [MATLAB Onramp](https://matlabacademy.mathworks.com/details/matlab-onramp/gettingstarted), a free 2 hour online tutorial that teaches the essentials of MATLAB.
%[text] %[text:anchor:H_8F8A032D] ![](text:image:4b73)   For an optimal experience, follow the instructions and steps in the given sequence. Proceed to a new section only after completing the preceding one. Some sections depend on variables created in prior sections and will generate errors if run out of order.
%[text] The ![Try this icon](text:image:84e9)  and  ![Exercise icon](text:image:5200) icons refer to two different types of interactive activities that you will find in this script. The ![Try this icon](text:image:3f81)  usually indicates an interaction where you will explore the visualization of some concept introduced in this script. The ![Exercise icon](text:image:9d74) interactions are designed to challenge your understanding of those concepts and may be used for grading and completion checks by your professor.
